		<item>
		<title>Andrade El Idolo reveals pitch made prior to WWE departure</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397064-andrade-el-idolo-reveals-pitch-made-prior-to-wwe-departure/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397064-andrade-el-idolo-reveals-pitch-made-prior-to-wwe-departure/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 23:46:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Andrade El Idolo]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[contract dispute]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[creative pitch]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397064</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>During an interview on Talk is Jericho, Andrade El Idolo spoke on the circumstances surrounding his departure from&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397064-andrade-el-idolo-reveals-pitch-made-prior-to-wwe-departure/">Andrade El Idolo reveals pitch made prior to WWE departure</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">During an interview on <a href="https://open.spotify.com/episode/0o67n0BBrICiCTwx5mFE9q">Talk is Jericho</a>, Andrade El Idolo spoke on the circumstances surrounding his departure from WWE in 2025.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">El Idolo explained that his return to the company the prior year was partly motivated by then-wife Charlotte Flair, wanting to be around to support her during her recovery from knee injury, but the subsequent divorce and certain creative pitches from WWE led to his decision to leave:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I went back to WWE to work with my ex-wife, and now that I’m divorced I felt a little weird. I wasn’t feeling at home or comfy. The story they gave, it wasn’t a good or specific good story or direction. Later, they wanted to send me to AAA. ‘Hey Andrade, It’s a good opportunity.’ I moved here to work with WWE.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I know AAA and respect AAA, I’ve respect for all the other companies but WWE is worldwide, and AAA is just in Mexico. People in Mexico know me. I wanted people to know me around the world, like in Australia, Arabia, Europe, and other countries where WWE have, where you can see on TV or Netflix or whatever. But it’s like back to Mexico and this for me like I prefer working in AEW and enjoy it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I made my name in Mexico so why go back to Mexico? I wanted to work in WWE with the top guys. It’s little things like no, I didn’t feel good…We were talking, I didn’t feel comfortable here. We talked and they gave me my release.</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Legal complications led to a disruption of his televised appearances for AEW, which finally came to an end after El Idolo worked with WWE to resolve issues surrounding a one-year non-compete clause.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Source: <a href="https://www.f4wonline.com/news/wwe/aew-star-walked-away-from-wwe-after-they-revealed-plans-for-him-in-aaa/">F4WOnline</a></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397064-andrade-el-idolo-reveals-pitch-made-prior-to-wwe-departure/">Andrade El Idolo reveals pitch made prior to WWE departure</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397064-andrade-el-idolo-reveals-pitch-made-prior-to-wwe-departure/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Report: Update on scrapped WWE Crown Jewel match</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 21:54:25 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Crown Jewel]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Premium Live Event]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Riyadh]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Saudi Arabia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397061</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>New details have emerged on the decision to scrap a planned match at WWE Crown Jewel on 11/7.&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/">Report: Update on scrapped WWE Crown Jewel match</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">New details have emerged on the decision to scrap a planned match at WWE Crown Jewel on 11/7.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A new report from <a href="https://www.f4wonline.com/news/wwe/subscriber-exclusive-wwe-star-opted-not-to-go-to-saudi-arabia-for-crown-jewel/">F4WOnline</a> has revealed that a bout between Gunther and Finn Balor was ultimately dropped from the premium live event&#8217;s lineup because Gunther decided against traveling to Saudi Arabia.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Multiple WWE sources reportedly confirmed the former World Heavyweight Champion&#8217;s decision was responsible for the change, with one source indicating that the situation went back and forth behind the scenes leading to the continued angles on television despite the bout&#8217;s uncertainty.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It was also noted that Balor had reservations about making the trip, though the belief internally is that he would have traveled had Gunther agreed to participate.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The situation is noteworthy given the perception among WWE talent that declining to work the events in Saudi Arabia was no longer an option.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/">Report: Update on scrapped WWE Crown Jewel match</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397061-report-update-on-scrapped-wwe-crown-jewel-match/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>Former WWE talent confirms departure from MLW</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397054-former-wwe-talent-confirms-departure-from-mlw/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397054-former-wwe-talent-confirms-departure-from-mlw/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 19:48:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[departure]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Dijak]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[MLW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397054</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>39-year-old Dijak (former WWE talent Dominik Dijakovic) has confirmed reports he has departed MLW and is a free&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397054-former-wwe-talent-confirms-departure-from-mlw/">Former WWE talent confirms departure from MLW</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">39-year-old Dijak (former WWE talent Dominik Dijakovic) has confirmed reports he has departed MLW and is a free agent, following his contract expiring. He was also known as T-Bar during his time in WWE when he was part of the Retribution faction from 2020-2022. Prior to the main roster, he spent 2017 to 2020 on the NXT roster. He left WWE on June 28, 2024 after his contract expired.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In his lengthy post on social media, he had nothing but good things to say about his time in MLW and that a the next presentation of his character will be &#8220;brand new and extraordinarily unique&#8221;, which he also said will debut &#8220;very soon.&#8221; Dijak also noted he is currently taking bookings. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">&#8220;<em>After much thought and consideration, I have decided that this past weekend was my final appearances for MLW and I will be entering Free Agency moving forward. I am incredibly grateful for my time in MLW, over the past two years I was given an exceptional platform to showcase my abilities as both a singles and tag team wrestler. I was able to capture gold as The Skyscrapers alongside my good friend and tag partner Baron Corbin. I was also able to have incredible matches against Killer Kross, Josh Bishop, Matt Riddle, Krule, Kevin Knight, The Good Brothers, Kenta, and many, many more. Thank you so much to Court Bauer for providing me with such an amazing place to call home.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>I am so very excited for the next chapter of my career moving forward. I have been wrestling all over the world at an incredibly high level, and I just knew it was time to truly bet on myself. I’m so excited to keep working with incredible independent companies like Progress, Limitless, Juggalo Championship, PW Rebellion, Blood Sweat Tears, and so many other amazing indy companies.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>2027 is going to be an unbelievably exciting year for me. I am going to be debuting a brand new and extraordinarily unique character presentation very soon, and I’m so excited to share my vision with all of you. I know deep down in my heart that I am currently the best I have ever been in the ring and I can’t wait to continue to showcase my passion and dedication for as many people as possible.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Thank you all so much for your continued support. It truly means the world to me.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Now it’s time to Feast Your Eyes on the Dijak Hijack of Free Agency.</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>BookDijak@gmail.com</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>KNOCK KNOCK</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>Dijak</em>&#8220;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">I have finished up with MLW and I am now a Free Agent<br><br>BookDijak@gmail.com <a href="https://t.co/sFtxOBH3mF">pic.twitter.com/sFtxOBH3mF</a></p>&mdash; DONOVAN DIJAK (@DijakFYE) <a href="https://x.com/DijakFYE/status/2119814558709854386?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 9, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397054-former-wwe-talent-confirms-departure-from-mlw/">Former WWE talent confirms departure from MLW</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/397054-former-wwe-talent-confirms-departure-from-mlw/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>John Cena reveals new details for the John Cena Classic</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397047-john-cena-reveals-new-details-for-the-john-cena-classic/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397047-john-cena-reveals-new-details-for-the-john-cena-classic/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 19:29:51 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[John Cena]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[John Cena Classic]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397047</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In speaking exclusively to The Takedown on SI, WWE&#8217;s John Cena revealed new details for the John Cena&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397047-john-cena-reveals-new-details-for-the-john-cena-classic/">John Cena reveals new details for the John Cena Classic</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In speaking exclusively to <a href="https://www.si.com/fannation/wrestling/features/john-cena-reveals-new-details-about-the-upcoming-john-cena-classic-exclusive" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">The Takedown on SI</a>, WWE&#8217;s John Cena revealed new details for the John Cena Classic, while clearing up some misconceptions about the event next month.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cena said it will not not feature a bracket-style tournament, as some fans had speculated. It will instead be  centered around a series of exhibition matches, much like how it was determined who is final opponent was for his retirement match last December. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>&#8220;They&#8217;re all gonna be current [main roster stars] versus NXT. It&#8217;s very much like Saturday Night&#8217;s Main Event, and I love that December 14th is the date, because that&#8217;s one year and one day from my last match. And as soon as I retired, on the way home, I was thinking about how I can [stay] involved.&#8221;</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Cena also stated in the interview, the Classic idea and concept was taken from other mainstream sporting events. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><em>&#8220;I wanna try to create [something like] an Arnold Classic. I took a lot from the Arnold Classic. I took a lot from fan appreciation nights. I took a lot from All-Star games, but I wanna create that situation where fans can come to an event they know every year, they know what the situation is, and we&#8217;re in the pilot.&#8221;</em></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">At the time of this writing, Cody Rhodes and Zilla Fatu are first two participants invited to the John Cena Classic.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The John Cena Classic will take place during a second episode of Monday Night Raw on December 14 at the ESPN Wild World Of Sports Complex at Walt Disney World in Orlando, Florida. The first-ever Cena Classic champion will be awarded a belt that is similar to his old WWE spinner championship belt. Those who are WWE Club Members will get to vote on John Cena Classic participants.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397047-john-cena-reveals-new-details-for-the-john-cena-classic/">John Cena reveals new details for the John Cena Classic</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397047-john-cena-reveals-new-details-for-the-john-cena-classic/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>AEW announces Thanksgiving edition of Collision</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397043-aew-announces-thanksgiving-edition-of-collision/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397043-aew-announces-thanksgiving-edition-of-collision/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 07:42:40 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Collision]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Thanksgiving]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397043</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>AEW has announced a special Thanksgiving edition of Collision, set to be taped on 11/25 after the Thanksgiving&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397043-aew-announces-thanksgiving-edition-of-collision/">AEW announces Thanksgiving edition of Collision</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">AEW has announced a special Thanksgiving edition of Collision, set to be taped on 11/25 after the Thanksgiving Eve edition of Dynamite and air the next night on the United States holiday.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The video on social media is narrated by Tony Schiavone and includes appearances from a number of AEW talents, along with a cameo appearance from non-contracted wrestlers Scott Garland (formerly Scotty 2 Hotty), Curry Man, and Glacier.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Aside from the change in night, Collision will air on TNT and HBO Max at 8:00 p.m. Eastern as usual.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The shows will emanate from the LFCU Arena in Omaha, Nebraska.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
https://twitter.com/AEW/status/2119444834364633465
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397043-aew-announces-thanksgiving-edition-of-collision/">AEW announces Thanksgiving edition of Collision</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397043-aew-announces-thanksgiving-edition-of-collision/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>TNA star reveals she was recently in a car accident, &#8220;so blessed to be alive!&#8221;</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397040-tna-reveals-she-was-recently-in-a-car-accident-so-blessed-to-be-alive/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397040-tna-reveals-she-was-recently-in-a-car-accident-so-blessed-to-be-alive/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 00:56:12 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Impact News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Jada Stone]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TNA]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397040</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>TNA talent Jade Stone revealed Sunday on her Instagram Stories that two days ago she was involved in&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397040-tna-reveals-she-was-recently-in-a-car-accident-so-blessed-to-be-alive/">TNA star reveals she was recently in a car accident, &#8220;so blessed to be alive!&#8221;</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">TNA talent Jade Stone revealed Sunday on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/stories/jada.stoneee/?hl=en" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">her Instagram Stories</a> that two days ago she was involved in a car accident that left her with several injuries. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Stone said she is &#8216;so blessed to be alive.&#8217;</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">TNA wrestler Jada Stone met with a car accident recently, wishing her a speedy recovery. <a href="https://t.co/AxczUPXrtz">pic.twitter.com/AxczUPXrtz</a></p>&mdash; Wrestle Sphere (@wrestlesphere0) <a href="https://x.com/wrestlesphere0/status/2119510833097216479?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 8, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397040-tna-reveals-she-was-recently-in-a-car-accident-so-blessed-to-be-alive/">TNA star reveals she was recently in a car accident, &#8220;so blessed to be alive!&#8221;</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/impact-wrestling-news/397040-tna-reveals-she-was-recently-in-a-car-accident-so-blessed-to-be-alive/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>WWE roster reportedly departed Saudi Arabia before missile attack on Riyadh</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397037-wwe-roster-reportedly-departed-saudi-arabia-before-missile-attack-on-riyadh/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397037-wwe-roster-reportedly-departed-saudi-arabia-before-missile-attack-on-riyadh/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 00:44:09 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[attacks]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Riyadh]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Saudi Arabia]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[WWE]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397037</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>PWInsider is reporting the WWE roster landed safely on Sunday in South Carolina, thus not affected by the&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397037-wwe-roster-reportedly-departed-saudi-arabia-before-missile-attack-on-riyadh/">WWE roster reportedly departed Saudi Arabia before missile attack on Riyadh</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.pwinsider.com/index.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">PWInsider</a> is reporting the WWE roster landed safely on Sunday in South Carolina, thus not affected by the <a href="https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/loud-booms-heard-saudi-capital-riyadh-after-early-warning-alert-issued-2026-11-08/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">attacks in Riyadh’s financial district</a>, including the Aramco skyscraper, which was damaged on Sunday after attacks done by Yemen’s Houthi rebel group.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Monday&#8217;s Raw takes place from the Bon Secours Wellness Arena in Greenville, South Carolina.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><a href="https://www.pwinsider.com/index.php" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">PWInsider</a> also reported there still may have been some staff in Riyadh helping with the break down of the production. At the time of the report there was no word if anyone associated with WWE still in the country was affected by Sunday’s attacks.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">It was also said that a majority the WWE roster actually flew into Bahrain, a neighboring country and then traveled from there by bus into Riyadh. The belief is some talents traveled in a private plane directly in and out of Riyadh.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397037-wwe-roster-reportedly-departed-saudi-arabia-before-missile-attack-on-riyadh/">WWE roster reportedly departed Saudi Arabia before missile attack on Riyadh</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/397037-wwe-roster-reportedly-departed-saudi-arabia-before-missile-attack-on-riyadh/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>International Championship Match added to AEW Full Gear PPV</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397024-international-championship-match-added-to-aew-full-gear-ppv/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397024-international-championship-match-added-to-aew-full-gear-ppv/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 04:38:49 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AEW News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Adam Copeland]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AEW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Full Gear]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[International Championship Match]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397024</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Kazuchika Okada defending the AEW International Championship has been added to next Saturday&#8217;s Full Gear pay-per-view. The men&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397024-international-championship-match-added-to-aew-full-gear-ppv/">International Championship Match added to AEW Full Gear PPV</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Kazuchika Okada defending the AEW International Championship has been added to next Saturday&#8217;s Full Gear pay-per-view.  The men competed in Blood and Guts last Wednesday. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back on the October 21 episode of Dynamite, Copeland teamed with Will Ospreay against Kyle Fletcher and Kevin Knight, that saw Okada interfere and then putting the International Championship belt on a turnbuckle which then saw Copeland hit his head on, costing Copeland and Ospreay the match.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Below is the current lineup for Full Gear. </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW World Championship Match: Will Ospreay defends against Kyle Fletcher</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW Women’s World Championship Match: Mercedes Mone defends against Marina Shafir</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW World Tag Team Championship Match: Young Bucks (Matt Jackson and Nick Jackson) defends against Mark Davis and Jake Doyle of the Don Callis Family</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW Women’s World Tag Team Championship Match: The Brawling Birds (Jamie Hayter and Alex Windsor) defends against Wrathlander (Kris Statlander and Harley Cameron)</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW World Trios Championships Texas Death Match: Hangman Page, Brody King and Bandido defend against Swerve Strickland &amp; The New Level (Kofi and Austin Creed) </p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-AEW International Championship Match: Kazuchika Okada defends against Adam Copeland</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Anarchy in the Arena: The Death Riders an The Conglomeration vs. The Cut </p>


<p>AEW Full Gear airs live on pay-per-view on Saturday, November 14 from the Mortgage Matchup Center in Phoenix, Arizona.</p><p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397024-international-championship-match-added-to-aew-full-gear-ppv/">International Championship Match added to AEW Full Gear PPV</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/aew-news/397024-international-championship-match-added-to-aew-full-gear-ppv/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>MLW Saturday Night Superfight Quick Results &#8211; 11/7/26 (New Champion Crowned, Court Bauer teases &#8220;Special Project&#8221; for 2027)</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/397018-mlw-saturday-night-superfight-quick-results-11-7-26-new-champion-crowned-court-bauer-teases-special-project-for-2027/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/397018-mlw-saturday-night-superfight-quick-results-11-7-26-new-champion-crowned-court-bauer-teases-special-project-for-2027/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Jerome Wilen]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 04:21:38 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Misc. News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[11/7 MLW Saturday Superfight Quick Results]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[MLW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Saturday Superfight]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=397018</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Below are the quick results from the MLW Saturday Night Superfight from the sold-out Cicero Stadium in Cicero,&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/397018-mlw-saturday-night-superfight-quick-results-11-7-26-new-champion-crowned-court-bauer-teases-special-project-for-2027/">MLW Saturday Night Superfight Quick Results &#8211; 11/7/26 (New Champion Crowned, Court Bauer teases &#8220;Special Project&#8221; for 2027)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Below are the quick results from the MLW Saturday Night Superfight from the sold-out <a href="https://mlw.com/2026/11/06/saturday-night-superfight-preview/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cicero Stadium</a> in Cicero, Illinois, which streamed live on VEEPS.  MLW Founder Court Bauer also teased a &#8220;special project&#8221; for 2027.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-MLW Tag Team Championships – Street Fight: Good Brothers (Karl Anderson and Doc Gallows) defeated Glasgow Boys On Top (Joe Coffey and Mark Coffey to retain.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Masha Slamovich def. ZAMAYA</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Tessa Blanchard def. Keyra</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-MLW National Openweight Championship: Austin Aries vs. Matt Riddle ended in a 30-minute time limit draw. Aries said he knows everyone wants five more minutes and says know. Riddle knocks him out and takes the title.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Ultimo Guerrero def. Templario and Titan</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Court Bauer thanks everyone attending. He brings out NJPW Chairman Naoki Sugabayashi. Court says MLW, NJPW, and CMLL are working on a big surprise for 2027 before introducing Yota Tsuji.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">MLW <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f91d.png" alt="🤝" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> NJPW<br><br>BIG things are coming!!<br><br>Order now: <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1f4fa.png" alt="📺" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <a href="https://t.co/BISft0S5FV">https://t.co/BISft0S5FV</a> <a href="https://t.co/QdJgp1eKNT">pic.twitter.com/QdJgp1eKNT</a></p>&mdash; MLW (@MLW) <a href="https://x.com/MLW/status/2119262618515014141?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 8, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Yota Tsuji def. Trevor Lee</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-MLW Championship – Last Man Standing: Josh Bishop def. Killer Kross to become the new champion</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list"></ul>



<figure class="wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-x wp-block-embed-x"><div class="wp-block-embed__wrapper">
<blockquote class="twitter-tweet" data-width="550" data-dnt="true"><p lang="en" dir="ltr">THE BLOOD KING’S REIGN IS OVER!<a href="https://x.com/JoshuaBishop_?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">@JoshuaBishop_</a> is the Last Man Standing!<br><br>Replay <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/17.0.2/72x72/1fa78.png" alt="🩸" class="wp-smiley" style="height: 1em; max-height: 1em;" /> <a href="https://t.co/BISft0S5FV">https://t.co/BISft0S5FV</a> <a href="https://t.co/Da6J5LB5Up">pic.twitter.com/Da6J5LB5Up</a></p>&mdash; MLW (@MLW) <a href="https://x.com/MLW/status/2119275694249386101?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw">November 8, 2026</a></blockquote><script async src="https://platform.x.com/widgets.js" charset="utf-8"></script>
</div></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Source: <a href="https://www.fightful.com/wrestling/mlw-saturday-night-superfight-results-11-7-killer-kross-yota-tsuji-tessa-blanchard-compete/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Fightful</a></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/misc-news/397018-mlw-saturday-night-superfight-quick-results-11-7-26-new-champion-crowned-court-bauer-teases-special-project-for-2027/">MLW Saturday Night Superfight Quick Results &#8211; 11/7/26 (New Champion Crowned, Court Bauer teases &#8220;Special Project&#8221; for 2027)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
